## Findings

### Critical — Recovery can still force-close a tab containing an untracked live host

`oc_live` and `pi_live` are set only after `wait_host_group` and PGID parsing succeed. If `herdr pane run` starts a host but either of those later steps fails, the ERR trap treats that host as inactive. It can check PGID `-1`, clean based on an invalid group identity, and close the tab once both flags read `0`, without proving the launched pane returned to its shell or its real process group is empty. Record a separate “launch submitted” state immediately after each successful `pane run`; an unclassified launch must retain its pane/root/tab for rework. Tab closure and root deletion must require positive shell-return and process/group-absence evidence for every submitted launch.

### High — Failed protected checkpoints are misclassified as retryable media candidates

`certify_media_candidate` now propagates the first pre-toggle checkpoint as status `2`, but a failed post-toggle checkpoint is stored in `post_rc`, and a failed restore checkpoint is stored in `restore_post_rc`; after exact playback restoration either case returns `1`. The outer loop then selects another source and may eventually launch hosts despite missing/failed PID/generation/socket/peer evidence around an earlier direct control. These are protected-boundary failures, not evidence that a source was merely uncontrollable. Return the hard-blocker status for any checkpoint failure and allow candidate retry only when every checkpoint succeeded and the candidate is proven unchanged/restored.

### High — UI verification still does not prove one coherent music status

`assert_ui` independently searches the entire viewport for truncated title text, truncated artist text, and a play/pause glyph. Those values can originate in different UI regions. The Pi uniqueness check only counts title-prefix occurrences, not music status components. It therefore cannot establish that each host renders identity and state together or that Pi has exactly one status after launch and `/reload`. Assert the complete extension-specific status row/region with identity and marker together, and count that representation exactly once for Pi.
